<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghent Altarpiece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1432">1432</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Adoration of the Mystic Lamb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a> Altarpiece, or Adoration of the Mystic Lamb, is a large folding polyptych in St Bavo's Cathedral, Ghent, completed in 1432. An inscription credits it to Hubert van Eyck and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-eyck">Jan van Eyck</a>. Its oil technique, detailed realism and complex religious programme made it one of the most influential works of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-netherlandish-painting">Early Netherlandish painting</a>, and it has been stolen, damaged and restored several times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghent-altarpiece.jpg" alt="Ghent Altarpiece" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan van Eyck / Presumably Hubert van Eyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghent_Altarpiece_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
